know about this so they can set up credentials or use a different method.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"74c63bf9e2c8069824a10ba30f4352e0cd10627893511902dc846d1eb36adac5\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n\\n备份失败：Git push 认证失败，无法连接到 GitHub。\\n\\n需要修复 Git 认证方式，可以用以下任一方法：\\n\\n1. **设置 SSH 密钥**（推荐）\\n2. **配置 credentials helper**：`git config --global credential.helper store`\\n\\n或者先检查现有配置：\\n```bash\\ngit remote -v\\ncat ~/.gitconfig\\n```\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"minimax-portal\",\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"usage\":{\"input\":12947,\"output\":124,\"cacheRead\":16832,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":29903,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779667474531,\"responseId\":\"0662c513410dfeb9d3907b01a88f0a02\"}}[... 3672 more characters truncated]"}],"details":{"persistedDetailsTruncated":true,"originalDetailsBytesAtLeast":8193,"originalDetailKeys":["status","exitCode","durationMs","aggregated","cwd"],"status":"completed","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus","exitCode":0},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779787486921}}
{"type":"message","id":"3875e405","parentId":"ac9b4055","timestamp":"2026-05-26T09:25:42.294Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the situation. Let me piece this together:\n\n1. The `daily-backup` cron job runs on agent `main`, uses MiniMax-M2.7 model\n2. On 2026-05-25 at 00:00 UTC, it ran successfully via exec to do `git add`, `git commit`, `git push` - the commit succeeded but the push failed with `fatal: could not read Username for 'https://github.com': No such device or address`\n3. Then there were two retry errors: `overloaded_error` from minimax-portal (\"server is busy, please retry later\")\n4. The final attempt handled the git push failure and reported to user\n\nBut the current error in the reply target is about the cron job failing TODAY (2026-05-26) with `EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released`.\n\nThis is a different error - it's a session file lock contention issue. The session file `84d5276f-896e-489d-a13a-0d020e1b1971.jsonl` was being used by another process (likely the main agent's ongoing conversation) when the cron job tried to take it over.\n\nThe issue is:\n1. **Root cause**: `daily-backup` is configured as a cron job targeting the **main agent's session** (sessionTarget=\"main\" or similar). When the main agent is already running a conversation (it's actively being used), the cron job can't take over the session because it's locked.\n2. This is a design issue - the backup job should use an **isolated session** instead of trying to take over the main session.\n\nLet me check the cron job configuration to confirm.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f92322e4d40b44788be10c94","name":"cron","arguments":{"action":"list","includeDisabled":true},"partialArgs":"{\"action\": \"list\", \"includeDisabled\": true}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779787486931,"responseId":"7bf46f925ec84f558aa71b25785ada95"}}
{"type":"message","id":"1561af31","parentId":"3875e405","timestamp":"2026-05-26T09:25:42.454Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f92322e4d40b44788be10c94","toolName":"cron","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"jobs\": [],\n  \"total\": 0,\n  \"offset\": 0,\n  \"limit\": 50,\n  \"hasMore\": false,\n  \"nextOffset\": null,\n  \"deliveryPreviews\": {}\n}"}],"details":{"jobs":[],"total":0,"offset":0,"limit":50,"hasMore":false,"nextOffset":null,"deliveryPreviews":{}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779787542450}}
{"type":"message","id":"5a03ef26","parentId":"1561af31","timestamp":"2026-05-26T09:27:07.795Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The cron job `daily-backup` failed with `EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError`. Let me understand what happened:\n\n1. The session file `84d5276f-896e-489d-a13a-0d020e1b1971.jsonl` exists and is from May 25 (last modified)\n2. Looking at the session content, it was a `daily-backup` cron job running on `main` agent\n3. The git commit succeeded (auto backup 2026-05-25), but git push failed because GitHub authentication wasn't configured\n4. Then the model (MiniMax-M2.7) returned overloaded errors twice\n5. Finally the agent reported the git push failure to the user\n\nBut the error message was `EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released`. This is a different error than the actual content of the session suggests. Let me think about this...\n\nThe error is saying that when the embedded prompt lock was released, the session file was changed. This typically happens when:\n- Two processes/agents try to write to the same session file concurrently\n- A cron job's session is running and another process modifies the session file\n\nThe cron job `daily-backup` runs on the `main` agent. The session file was being written to, and when the lock was released (for the embedded prompt tool call), the session file had been modified by something else (maybe another cron job or another agent run).\n\nWait, let me re-read the session data more carefully. The session shows the daily-backup ran at midnight (May 25 00:00 UTC). The git push failed because no credentials configured. The model then returned overloaded errors.\n\nBut the actual `EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError` message suggests a race condition - while the main agent was processing the embedded prompt in the cron job session, something else wrote to the same session file concurrently.\n\nThis is a known OpenClaw issue when multiple cron jobs or agent sessions target the same agent simultaneously. The session file lock mechanism detects that the file was modified while the lock was held, which prevents data corruption.\n\nLet me check if there are other cron jobs that might run at the same time, and check the current state.\n\nSince cron list returned empty (0 jobs), perhaps the cron jobs failed and were cleaned up, or they were configured differently. Let me check the openclaw config for cron jobs.\n\nActually, the cron list returned empty. This might mean the jobs are stored elsewhere. Let me check the gateway config.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9897b74985724dd48013bb05","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron list 2>&1 || echo \"no openclaw CLI\"","timeout":10},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"openclaw cron list 2>&1 || echo \\\"no openclaw CLI\\\"\", \"timeout\": 10}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a1eabde483fa4cafbe08e448","name":"gateway","arguments":{"action":"config.get","path":"cron"},"partialArgs":"{\"action\": \"config.get\", \"path\": \"cron\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779787542455,"responseId":"fa3fc7d869c74843b5dc2c9dca23994e"}}
