{"type":"message","id":"8a3daaf8","parentId":"426d3503","timestamp":"2026-05-26T11:00:26.342Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's already an SSH key (`id_ed25519`) in `~/.ssh/`. The repo is using HTTPS remote. I need to switch it to SSH. Let me check if the SSH key is added to GitHub by testing connection, then change the remote URL.\n\nThe SSH public key is: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAKNN9ZNTJ7zGOhpYVRTUUtwbf2IqzZF4SCKUO5XMLz block.lee121@gmail.com`\n\nLet me:\n1. Test SSH connection to GitHub\n2. If it works, change remote from HTTPS to SSH\n3. Retry the push","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"SSH key 已经存在了。改成 SSH "},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c726e9d82df64250ab587796","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -T git@github.com 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\"","timeout":15},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -T git@github.com 2>&1; echo \\\"EXIT:$?\\\"\", \"timeout\": 15}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779793206245,"responseId":"8c8d64dfacd04b9bac4c1990d655eb2b"}}
