{"type":"message","id":"d4738d10","parentId":"b7c98932","timestamp":"2026-05-26T11:01:58.219Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No root access. Can't install openssh-client. Let me think of another approach.\n\nOptions:\n1. Use credential helper to store the password/token in a file\n2. Use GIT_ASKPASS to provide credentials non-interactively\n3. Inject the SSH key via a different mechanism\n4. Use `git config --global url.\"git@github.com:\".insteadOf \"https://github.com/\"` but that needs ssh which we don't have\n5. Use `git config --global credential.helper store` and write a credentials file\n6. Use `GIT_ASKPASS` or a custom credential helper\n\nActually, there's no SSH client in the container and we can't install it. So the HTTPS approach with credential helper is the way to go.\n\nThe simplest approach: use `git config --global credential.helper store` and write a `.git-credentials` file with a token.\n\nBut we need a GitHub token. Let me check if there's one stored anywhere, or we could use the environment variable approach.\n\nWait, actually we could use `GIT_ASKPASS` to echo a token, or we could set up a credential helper that reads from a file.\n\nLet me check if git already has the credential-store helper available or if we can use GIT_ASKPASS.\n\nActually, the cleanest fix that doesn't need any new software:\n\n1. `git config --global credential.helper 'store --file ~/.git-credentials'`\n2. Write the credentials file: `https://username:token@github.com`\n\nBut we need a token. Let me search for any tokens or ask the user... Actually, the user said \"能不能干活\" (can you get to work / fix it), so they want me to fix it. Let me think about what tokens might be available.\n\nActually, we could also just set the remote URL to include credentials inline. But that's not great for the credentials file.\n\nWait, another approach: use environment variable or GIT_ASKPASS to pass the credentials. But we need a token.\n\nLet me check if the ssh key can be used without the ssh binary. Actually no, that won't work.\n\nLet me check if there's a GITHUB_TOKEN in any config file or env.\n\nHmm, the output showed `GITHUB_TOKEN=*** and `GH_TOKEN=*** as empty. Let me check if there are other tokens stored somewhere.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"SSH client 不在容器里"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_055580c71cfe407e83c8eaa4","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"git config --global credential.helper 'store --file ~/.git-credentials' && echo \"credential helper set\"","timeout":10},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"git config --global credential.helper 'store --file ~/.git-credentials' && echo \\\"credential helper set\\\"\", \"timeout\": 10}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ce951e8222554b54892295d6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"GITHUB\\|GH_TOKEN\\|github.*token\\|GIT.*TOKEN\" ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null; grep -r \"github\" ~/.openclaw/*.env 2>/dev/null; find ~ -name \"*.env\" -maxdepth 2 2>/dev/null | xargs grep -l \"GITHUB\\|GH_TOKEN\" 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; env | grep -i \"GITHUB\\|GIT.*TOKEN\" 2>/dev/null","timeout":10},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"grep -r \\\"GITHUB\\\\|GH_TOKEN\\\\|github.*token\\\\|GIT.*TOKEN\\\" ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null; grep -r \\\"github\\\" ~/.openclaw/*.env 2>/dev/null; find ~ -name \\\"*.env\\\" -maxdepth 2 2>/dev/null | xargs grep -l \\\"GITHUB\\\\|GH_TOKEN\\\" 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"---\\\"; env | grep -i \\\"GITHUB\\\\|GIT.*TOKEN\\\" 2>/dev/null\", \"timeout\": 10}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779793245392,"responseId":"976bf2e356bd4cd2a410e8d6b341a81e"}}
